# 22-dashboard-infographic-redesign

Read AGENTS.md first. Then read this entire file before writing code.

## §0 · WHAT THIS IS

The Dashboard currently renders three number tiles, a flat "Needs attention" table and a
20-row activity log. See @prompt_material/16-dashboard-current.png. It displays data but
does not explain it. The single most important fact on that screen — 20 of 22 chapters
have no narration — is buried in a tile labelled by its negative.

Rebuild the Dashboard as a production-readiness view: what is finished, what is blocked,
and what to work on next, legible in about three seconds.

This is a REDESIGN of one screen. Scope boundaries in §10.

## §0.1 · STOP GATE — DEPENDENCY APPROVAL

This work needs a charting library. Recommendation: **recharts**, via the shadcn/ui Chart
component, because you already use shadcn and its chart primitives are built on Recharts
with composition in mind — you compose Recharts elements and theme them through CSS
variables, so the existing token system carries over intact.

AGENTS.md forbids adding a dependency without explicit approval. STOP here. Report the
recommendation, the approximate bundle cost, and wait.

If approval is DENIED, build every visual in §3–§6 with CSS only. Stacked bars, progress
bars and the sparkline are all achievable with flex widths and a small inline SVG
polyline. Say so and proceed — a denial is not a blocker, it changes the technique.

Do not install anything else. No D3, no Chart.js, no animation library, no icon pack.

