## §2 · STEP 2 — AGGREGATION

§2.1 Extend lib/catalog.ts with pure functions. No React, no I/O, deterministic:

readinessBreakdown(chapters): { ready, textOnly, audioOnly, empty }
ready = script_text present AND audio_path present
textOnly = script present, audio missing
audioOnly = audio present, script missing
empty = both missing
The four buckets are mutually exclusive and must sum to the chapter total.
Assert that in a unit-free runtime check; if it fails, that is a data bug worth
surfacing rather than hiding.

bookReadiness(book, chapters): the same four counts scoped to one book, plus a
percentComplete derived from ready / total.

accessMix(chapters): { free, locked }

activityByDay(entries, days): an array of { date, count } covering the last N days
inclusive, with zero-filled gaps. Zero-filling matters — a missing day must render
as a zero-height column, not be skipped, or the axis lies.

§2.2 Extend lib/queries.ts:

getReadinessCounts() — one aggregate query, not a full chapter fetch
getPerBookReadiness() — id, title, and the four counts per book
getAccessMix()
getActivityByDay(14) — derived from activity_log.created_at

Select only the columns each aggregate needs. Do NOT pull script_text to test whether
it is null — use a boolean projection. Pulling 22 chapters of prose to count them is
the exact mistake prompt 13 was written to avoid.

§2.3 No schema change. No new tables. No new columns. No migration.

§2.4 There is no historical snapshot table, so no chart may claim to show completion
trending over time. The only honest time series available is event counts from
activity_log. Do not fabricate a trend, a delta, a "+3 this week", or an arrow.

## §3 · STEP 3 — ROW 1, READINESS STRIP

The hero element. Full container width, one card, directly below the page header.

§3.1 Heading "Production readiness", 16px/600. Sub-line, 12px muted, computed:
"<ready> of <total> chapters ready to publish."

§3.2 One horizontal stacked bar, full card width, 40px tall, 8px radius, four segments in
this order: Ready, Text only, Audio only, Empty. Segment widths proportional to
count. Segments under 4% of the width still render at a 4px minimum so they never
vanish — a single blocked chapter must remain visible.

§3.3 Colours, from existing tokens only:
Ready status-ok
Text only status-warn
Audio only primary
Empty border, with muted text
Never encode meaning by colour alone. Every segment carries a legend entry below the
bar with a colour chip, the label, and the count: "Ready 2 · Text only 18 ·
Audio only 0 · Empty 2". Hovering a segment shows a tooltip with the same text.

§3.4 A percentage reads at the right of the heading row, 24px/600: ready / total as a
whole number. Frame it positively — completion, not deficiency.

## §4 · STEP 4 — ROW 2, METRIC TILES

Keep three tiles, keep the existing tile geometry and 24px gaps. Change what they say.

§4.1 Tile 1 — BOOKS. The count. Sub-line: "<n> published · <n> draft".
§4.2 Tile 2 — CHAPTERS. The count. Sub-line: "<n> free · <n> locked".
§4.3 Tile 3 — AUDIO COVERAGE. Replace "MISSING AUDIO". Show "<n>/<n>" in mono at the same
size as the other tile numbers, with a 4px progress bar beneath at the tile's width.
Bar fill is status-ok above 80%, status-warn between 20% and 80%, destructive below
20%. Sub-line: "<n> chapters still need narration."

§4.4 Uppercase 13px/600 muted labels above the numbers, exactly as now. No sparklines in
tiles, no percentage deltas, no trend arrows (§2.4).

## §5 · STEP 5 — ROW 3, PER-BOOK COMPLETION

§5.1 Card headed "By book", sub-line "Where each story stands."

§5.2 One row per book: cover thumbnail at 24×36, title, then the same four-segment
stacked bar as §3.2 at 16px tall scoped to that book, then the percentage in mono at
the right on a fixed axis so the numbers align down the column.

§5.3 Row height 48px. Full row is a link to /books/<id>. Hover uses the existing table
row hover.

§5.4 Sort by percentComplete ascending — least finished first. That is the work queue
order and it is the point of the card.

§5.5 Cap at 8 rows with a footer link "View all in Books". Long titles truncate with an
ellipsis and carry a title attribute; they must never wrap the row to two lines.

## §6 · STEP 6 — ROW 4, TWO HALF-WIDTH CARDS

Side by side, 24px gap, equal width.

§6.1 Left — "Access mix". A single horizontal stacked bar, Free versus Locked, 24px tall,
with counts and percentages labelled beside it.

     Do NOT use a pie or donut. With two categories a stacked bar is more precise and more
     information-dense; pie charts only earn their place when a single simple proportion
     needs selling, and this is not that.

     Beneath it, one muted 12px line: "<n> locked chapters need an ad view or a
     subscription." Consistent with the existing access helper copy.

§6.2 Right — "Activity". A 14-day column chart from getActivityByDay. Columns in primary
at 60% opacity, today's column at full opacity. Y axis hidden; the shape is the
message and a labelled axis on counts this small is chartjunk. X axis labels only the
first, middle and last day. Tooltip on hover gives the date and the event count.

     Sub-line: "<n> events in the last 14 days."

     This chart measures operator activity, not content completion. Label it so nobody
     reads it as progress.

