## §10 · CONSTRAINTS

1.  Dashboard only — app/(dashboard)/page.tsx, its loading and error files, new
    components under components/dashboard/, and the §2 additions to lib/.
2.  Do not touch Books, Book editor, Chapter editor, Settings, Uploads, Bulk import,
    Clerk auth, any server action, or the mobile app.
3.  No schema change, no migration, no new columns, no new tables.
4.  Read-only. This screen performs no mutation.
5.  Page stays a Server Component and fetches the data. Charts are Client Components
    receiving fully-computed props — never raw rows, never a fetch in a chart.
6.  Every colour from the prompt-01 token set: page, card, border, primary, text, muted,
    sidebar, status-ok, status-warn, destructive. No new hex anywhere, including chart
    fills. Theme recharts through CSS variables, not literal colours.
7.  Flat surfaces. Max 1px borders. 8px card radius. 24px inter-card gap. 1040px
    container. 8px spacing grid. No shadows, no gradients, no glassmorphism.
8.  No animation beyond the chart library's default mount transition. No counting-up
    numbers, no parallax, no confetti.
9.  No gauges, speedometers, radar charts, treemaps, word clouds, or 3D anything.
10. Exactly one ember button on the screen: New book.
11. WCAG 2.2 AA contrast. Meaning never carried by colour alone (§3.3).
12. Strict TypeScript. No any. Chart props typed from the §2 return types.
13. Desktop only at 1440×1024.

